ally focusing on the m2 chip  for the macbook pro announcement and  here at the info page we see that it is  the same design and apple is really  pushing that m2 chip we have up to a 40  percent improvement in performance  compared to the m1 model six times  faster than intel of course and some  great battery life apple's saying a new  chip new chapter for the 13-inch macbook  pro but i don't really think that's true  because this same chip is available in  the macbook air and for the rest of the  macbook pro it is the old chapter this  is a design that came out in 2016.  and let me show you what else has  changed other than this ship and then  we're also going to talk about  throttling and if you really need that  fan for performance we have this  gorgeous retina display and apple is  saying see the better picture but in  reality you are not seeing the better  picture because this is the same display  that we've had for years and it still  only supports millions of colors 16.7  million compared to the m2 macbook air  that actually supports over a billion  colors now don't get me wrong this is  not a bad display  you still get 500 nits of brightness you  have better color accuracy p3 wide color  you have true tone that's nice and  convenient to switch to your environment  but the macbook pros always had a better  display than the macbook air but not  anymore now as far as cameras in  microphones you can be seen and be heard  but it's gonna be the exact same as  before and that was actually one of the  biggest weaknesses and complaints about  the previous m1 macbook pro it has a  720p webcam built in here's how it looks  like compared to the new 1080p cameras  that is actually what's coming in the  macbook air so that hasn't changed it's  a shocking difference now as far as  microphones those also have not changed  whereas the macbook air they've updated  those ones here's what it sounded like  before this is the microphone quality of  the m1 macbook airs microphones and the  m2 macbook air has upgraded microphones  and this is the quality of the m1  macbook pros microphones and they're  staying the same with the m2 macbook pro  the macbook air's microphone is actually  quite a bit louder than the macbook pros  studio microphone but i do think the  studio does sound a little bit less  boomy now as far as speakers the  speakers in here are exactly the same  they're not bad but what is shocking is  that the macbook air previously actually  sounded better it was both louder and  had better bass than the macbook pro go  ahead and take a listen  now with this new 2022 m2 macbook pro  the speakers have not changed they are  identical and i don't want to make this  a full-on comparison to the new macbook  air but that one has quad speakers now  they're going to fire upwards towards  the screen and through the keyboard  they're gonna sound even better now  personally seeing as none of these core  things and things that were an issue  before have changed that is quite a bit  of a disappointment if you're spending  this much money and a lot of people are  going to start upgrading the ssd and the  ram as well now i'll go into those  configurations and my thoughts on it but  when we take a look at this design if  you're spending that much money on a  laptop that you are going to have for  many years do you really want to have  this older design i mean maybe if you  love the touch bar that is one reason to  buy it but the fact that has an older  keyboard layout it also only has two  thunderbolt ports just like before you  don't have a mac safe charger for that  extra convenience and to free up a port  for you to use we don't have an sd card  reader included like we do with the 14  inch macbook pro and other than that  nothing at all has changed so we know  that this is going to be the next  macbook pro that's going to be replaced  as soon as apple can now i know some of  you guys can say man this has the fan  you are going to get better performance  than the macbook air and that is  absolutely correct apple's own charge  show that is 1.4 times faster compared  to 1.3 times faster with the macbook air  now of course if you're doing simple  tasks like most people do or even short  bursts during 4k editing with short  bursts of rendering that's not going to  be hugely taxing and like i mentioned  with the previous macbook air it was not  that much slower for heavy long  intensive tasks for example exporting  high resolution raw images when you're  waiting close to half hour a couple  minutes isn't a huge deal breaker and  that's also including the cheaper 7 core  model not the a core this time around we  will see how the thermal performance  does with the macbook air and also if  we're going to be able to hack it like  we did with the m1 macbook air add those  thermal pads and get it to actually  outperform the macbook pro which kind of  blows your mind how is that possible  well that's possible because apple  doesn't actually ramp up the fan soon  enough so the macbook pro does actually  throttle whereas the one that's fanless  there's no fan to adjust so when we  added a thermal pad it actually  outperformed it if you guys want to see  us using the thermal pad hack on the new  macbook air make sure you click that  subscribe button so you guys don't miss  out on that video when we look at the  full detailed specifications  what has changed other than that chip  nothing i mean the only thing they're  doing now is giving you a 67 watt  charger instead of a 61 watt charger the  battery life is the same the battery is  the same the screen speakers every  single thing is the same as well as the  prices now i know some people say i'm  buying that just because i want the fan  i want to get the maximum performance  but honestly if you're somebody that  really cares about the performance once  you grab one of these and you add the  ram because you need more ram if you  care about performance and productivity  you upgrade your storage now you're only  looking at a 300 difference compared to  the 14 inch macbook pro that not only  has way better microphones speakers  webcam it also has the larger display  that's 1000 nits sustained up to 1600  nits for hdr you have three thunderbolt  ports a separate charger you have a sd  card reader you have dual fans built in  that will actually run quieter so once  you add those you are getting so much  more bang for your buck spending a  little bit more and getting more  graphics performance and more processor  performance as well so if you're  somebody that's buying the m2 macbook  pro because of the performance and  you're going to be upgrading it i would  say don't buy it anyways spend a little  bit more money and get yourself a 14  inch that is redesigned and that design  is going to stick around for at least  another five years  with those extras and not get quickly  replaced so why in the world did apple  keep this outdated macbook and they're  selling it for the same price and they  just put the m2 chip in there well i  think it's for two reasons the first one  is because of profit margins they're  gonna make more money selling this old  macbook the way it's been for a long  time than the redesigned m2 version it  is gonna be a lot of money for them they  don't have to have that expensive screen  with the cutouts they don't have to have  mac safe included into it it's not a new  chassis none of that it's the old one  and two just to get people to want to  upgrade from it once they add those  extra you know the storage and ram to  the 14 inch model i mean even if you go  on their website and you click on  macbook pro you see that they have it on  the left hand side looking all dinky and  small and they actually put the 16 inch  closer to it which they usually don't do  and then the 14 inch to make you want to  buy that instead and that gets you to  spend more money which is true but at  the same time you are getting that  better laptop now if you're somebody  that doesn't need the high-end upgrades  that's where i would say take a look  once again at buying either something  that's lower like this or the redesigned  m2 macbook air that's also going to  stick around for a long time and does  have a screen that supports over a  billion colors and has the extra max  save charging and the other updates as  well you guys let me know your thoughts  down below we are also going to be doing  a direct comparison on those two  macbooks so if you guys want to see the  m2 macbook air vs m2 macbook pro in  detail click that circle above check out  one of those great videos right over  there this has been max and i'll see you  in the next video  [Music]
 

